# Real Lightroom evidence, for the `#[ignore]`d tests only.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in one pair of paths. `.env` is gitignored:
# real catalog paths and real catalog bytes never enter the repo.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   sh scripts/check.sh real
#
# Every worktree on a machine needs this gate, so a second route exists that no
# worktree owns: put the same two names in `~/.config/lrsalvage/real.env` (or the
# file named by `git config lrsalvage.realEnvFile`). A worktree's own `.env` wins
# where it exists; the machine's file is the fallback.
#
# The catalog and its cache must be the same pair — `<name>.lrcat` beside
# `<name> Previews.lrdata` — and only that pair is opened, read-only.
#
# What these tests are for: they are the only source of the "verified" rows in
# README.md's compatibility table, and of the evidence labels in
# docs/format-notes.md. A layout measured from real files is a fact; the same
# layout asserted from a synthetic vault is a decision. Do not upgrade a claim
# without running these.

LRSALVAGE_TEST_CATALOG=""
LRSALVAGE_TEST_PREVIEWS=""
